    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="43">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 43</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">Ac uton don swa us þea[r]f is: uton niman us to bisnan þæt ærran worldwitan to ræde geræddon, Æþelstan ⁊ Eadmund ⁊ Eadgar þe nihst wæs, hu hi God weorðodon ⁊ Godes lage heoldon ⁊ Godes gafel læstan, þa hwile þe hi leofodon.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">But let us do what is our duty, let us take as our example what the secular authorities of old wisely decreed—Æthelstan and Edmund and Edgar, who came last—how they honoured God and kept his law and rendered tribute to him as long as they lived.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
